# Phase NM1: near-miss search in the why-not kernel

**Status: draft r1, awaiting owner review; implementable once the plan and this
spec are approved.**

## Provenance

- Plan: [why-not-near-misses-plan.md](why-not-near-misses-plan.md) r1, §2.1 and
  §4 NM1. No review has run over the plan or this spec.
- Inherited: derivation-why-not WN1 spec and record (kernel, oracle, budgets),
  WN-R1..R8.
- Tag `(o1)`: the owner's direction of 2026-11-01 (quoted in the plan), which
  covers NM-D3, D4 and D5. NM-D6 is the plan author's proposal.

## Obligations

| Source | Obligation | Discharged in |
|---|---|---|
| Plan O1 | join variables of an empty join | §6 `roles` per pair |
| Plan O2 | values from each side differing by case, whitespace, punctuation | §6 `_normalize`, `_near_misses` |
| Plan O3, NM-R1 | exact matching unchanged | §6 invariant; T7, T9 |
| Plan O4 | spelling gap distinguishable from missing fact | §6 empty list vs pairs; T2, T3 |
| Plan O5 | covers what host case-folding covers, and more | T1 |
| Plan O7 | redacted view hides values | §6 view; T10 |
| Plan O9, NM-R3 | bounded, counted | §6 charges; T11, T12 |
